---
// src/pages/_site-updates/2026-10-26-applications-and-screening.astro
export const updateMeta = {
  date: '2026-10-26',
  title: 'New workflow page: Applications & Screening',
  tags: ['workflows', 'applications', 'screening', 'waitlist', 'seo'],
};
---
<article class="border-l-4 border-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] pl-6">
  <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">October 26, 2026</h2>
  <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-4">
    Added an Applications &amp; Screening workflow page at
    <a href="/workflows/applications-and-screening" class="text-[hsl(24,95%,53%)] hover:underline">/workflows/applications-and-screening</a>
    covering Application Links, the screening questionnaire builder, importing an existing application form, and reviewing and approving applicants.
  </p>

  <div class="mb-4">
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">New file</h3>
    <ul class="text-sm text-gray-600 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1">
      <li><code>src/pages/workflows/applications-and-screening.astro</code>: Application Links (public link, QR code, website embed, email-code confirmation, source tracking, stop, pause, replace, and revoke), the screening template builder, form import including Google Sites embeds, reviewing prospects, Send Agreement First, and what approval gives an applicant. States that a waitlist application carries no signature. Includes FAQPage and HowTo structured data.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-semibold text-gray-900 mb-1">SEO</h3>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
      The new page is picked up by the generated sitemap on the next build. No screenshots yet; they follow separately.
    </p>
  </div>
</article>
